      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T22:45:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit. Why do we need the prefix in the enum value? Since it\u0027s a C++ enum type, couldn\u0027t we just do `BindingTypeOrder::DynamicBuffer` or something like that? (In which case the `BindingTypeOrder` part would be redundant?) I realize that the equivalent enum had this redundancy too, so maybe it\u0027s an enum to int/index thing that I\u0027m missing?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "2571cfeb9d8ed45d4d08217d7f172b22b8503888",
