        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 76,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-01T11:32:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need the prefix because it is a C-style enum that directly adds all of its enumerants to the enclosing namespace. Basically this is to avoid `SampledTexture` referring to the enum value instead of something else. The reason why it is a C enum instead of a C++ enum is because we want to do arithmetic on it [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.cpp;drc\u003dc07546451dd0b43c8d871dd9d3a69092dd8198f3;l\u003d1072) and [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.cpp;drc\u003dc07546451dd0b43c8d871dd9d3a69092dd8198f3;l\u003d701) in the enumerate. (I actually tried going to enum class before hitting this issue again)\n\nThe reason why there wasn\u0027t prefixed previously was because the enum was in the BindGroupLayoutInternalBase class and kinda namespaced thanks to that.",
      "parentUuid": "073341a7_70bbd25d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 21
      },
